@@ -0,0 +1,25 @@
+---
+id: dl-004-hourly-rentals-sub-day-utc-whole-hour-periods-priced-per-hour-only-for-items-with-an-hourlyprice
+type: decision-log
+title: "Hourly rentals: sub-day UTC whole-hour periods priced per hour, only for items with an hourlyPrice"
+status: pending
+---
+
+<!-- decision-log body. `wingfoil memory add` copies this scaffold verbatim; `memory submit` replaces
+     these placeholder comments with real content and fills the required frontmatter fields. -->
+
+## Context
+
+Visitors want a board for an afternoon. Periods were whole UTC days only.
+
+## Decision
+
+A period shorter than 24 hours is hourly: both ends must be UTC whole hours (it may cross midnight), and
+the total is hours times `hourlyPrice`. A period of 24 hours or more must still be UTC midnights, so
+10:00 to 10:00 the next day is rejected. Items without `hourlyPrice` reject hourly periods. The 3-day
+discount does not apply to hourly rentals. `availability` still takes whole days; hourly bookings block
+any day they touch, using the existing half-open overlap check.
+
+## Consequences
+
+Existing daily behaviour is unchanged. Hourly price is optional and independent of the daily price.
